// How far to scroll, in pixels and down positive, to bring the span from cvi_top to cvi_bot of a line of content into a window cvi_ch tall whose first row of content is cvi_sy, keeping cv_see_px pixels clear of the window's edges: 0 when it is in view; when the span is too tall for the window its top is what shows.
// By hand: a span from 300 to 320 in a window of 150 whose content starts at 100 runs to 344 with its room, 94 below the window's end at 250, so 94 down; one from 60 to 80 lies 36 above the top at 100 with its room, so 64 up.
